      "reasoning": "I see what happened — I cast Rousing Read, but there's no legal target because it can only enchant *my* creatures, not my opponent's. I must have misclicked or misunderstood the targeting.\n\
\n\
Rousing Read says \"Enchant creature\" with no restriction, but the triggered ability (\"When this enters, draw two cards...\") triggers only if it enters the battlefield legally. However, upon closer inspection, the card doesn't specify controller — but in Magic, \"Enchant creature\" auras can only target creatures you can enchant, and you can't enchant opponent's creatures unless the card says so (like Animate Dead).\n\
\n\
Rousing Read doesn't have \"Enchant creature you control\", but it's implied by the game rules — you can't attach an aura to an opponent's creature unless it explicitly allows it.\n\
\n\
So my attempt to cast Rousing Read was invalid because I have no creatures in play to enchant.\n\
\n\
I should have cast Sylvan Brushstrider instead — I have two copies, but that’s fine. It’s a 3/2 for {2}{G} with a life gain trigger, excellent tempo.\n\
\n\
Let me correct that.\n\
\n\
I’ll pass priority, then replay my turn properly.\n\
\n\
\n\
