- Trufflesnout ({2}{G})  \n\
Also, Irresistible Prey ({G}) — a combat trick that forces my creature to be blocked and draws me a card.\n\
\n\
Best development: play the second Forest to maximize mana, then cast **two 2/2s or 3/2s** next turn.\n\
\n\
But I can only cast one creature now. I have two copies of Sylvan Brushstrider and one Trufflesnout.\n\
\n\
Trufflesnout offers flexibility: when it enters, I choose — either +1/+1 counter (making it 3/3) or gain 4 life (bringing me to 21). Given that I'm at 17 life and my opponent has a 3/3 flyer, gaining life could be valuable.\n\
\n\
But Brushstrider gives me immediate life (gain 2) and is a 3/2 — better than Trufflesnout's base 2/2.\n\
\n\
I should cast **Sylvan Brushstrider** now to get the biggest body and life gain. I can cast Trufflesnout next turn and choose the life gain option, pushing me to a safer life total.\n\
\n\
Sequence:\n\
- This turn: Play Forest, cast Sylvan Brushstrider (3/2, gain 2 → 19)\n\
- Next turn: Cast Trufflesnout, choose \"gain 4 life\" → 23\n\
\n\
