      "game_seq": 143,
      "reasoning": "I have one untapped Forest ({G}) remaining and can cast **Irresistible Prey** ({G}).  \n\
\n\
This card has two uses:  \n\
- Force my creature to be blocked (useful in combat)  \n\
- Draw a card  \n\
\n\
I don’t have another creature besides Sylvan Brushstrider, and my opponent has a tapped Benevolent Hydra. They’ll likely untap and attack again.  \n\
\n\
If I cast Irresistible Prey now and target Brushstrider, I can draw a card and ensure it gets blocked next turn — but I’m the active player, so combat isn’t coming up for me. Instead, **my opponent** will have combat first.  \n\
\n\
So if I want to draw a card and potentially force a block when *I* attack, I should wait until my turn when I can attack into a fresh board.  \n\
\n\
Casting it now just gives me the card draw, but no immediate combat benefit.  \n\
\n\
However, drawing a card is still valuable — I’m setting up for Ormos, and more gas helps.  \n\
\n\
Still, I can wait. I’ll hold it for next turn when I can attack with Brushstrider and potentially make it unblockable *or* force a block with the aura.  \n\
\n\
Best to keep mana open and preserve flexibility.  \n\
\n\
I’ll pass priority and move to combat.  \n\
\n\
I pass.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
