      "game_seq": 171,
      "reasoning": "The situation is dire.\n\
\n\
My opponent now has:\n\
- **Benevolent Hydra 6/6** (base 1/1 +1/+1 counter from Scale the Heights, +3/+3 from Impending Doom), flying, trample, **must attack each combat**\n\
- **Servant of the Scale 4/4** (2/2 base + two +1/+1 counters), a large ground threat\n\
- Multiple lands and only 3 cards in hand — could have removal or more threats\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- 19 life\n\
- One untapped Forest ({G})\n\
- Sylvan Brushstrider 3/2 (sick)\n\
- No way to interact with the 6/6 flying trampler\n\
\n\
Even if I cast **Trufflesnout** next turn and grow it, I won't have enough to block.\n\
\n\
My best path is to **develop board**, **gain life**, and **set up Ormos** quickly.\n\
\n\
Next turn:\n\
- I can play a land\n\
- Cast **Trufflesnout** ({2}{G}) — and choose **gain 4 life** → go to 23\n\
- Keep building toward Ormos\n\
\n\
With Tome Anima and Archive Keeper, I can trigger Ormos's enter effect (discard three different names) as early as turn 6.\n\
\n\
But if the 6/6 trample flyer attacks unblocked, it’s **6 damage per turn** — I’m dead in four hits.\n\
\n\
I need to stabilize.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- **Irresistible Prey** on Brushstrider next turn — not helpful\n\
- **Ormos** into discard outlet (e.g., sacrifice Tome Anima) to draw into answers?\n\
- Hope to draw removal?\n\
\n\
But no instant removal in hand.\n\
\n\
Best move: accept pressure and **race**.\n\
\n\
Play as many bodies and gain as much life as possible.\n\
\n\
I pass priority to end this turn — nothing more I can do.\n\
\n\
This reminds me of a game in Budapest — I was down to 8 life against a 7/7 flying menace, but I topdecked **Beast Within** and won. I need a topdeck now.\n\
\n\
I pass.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
