      "reasoning": "My opponent's **Benevolent Hydra 6/6 with flying and trample** is attacking me. I have no blockers, no instant-speed removal, and no way to prevent damage.\n\
\n\
I will take **6 damage** — life total goes from 19 to **13**.\n\
\n\
This is critical. At 13 life, I have very little margin for error. Another attack from the Hydra next turn could be lethal unless I stabilize.\n\
\n\
I must use every resource to develop:\n\
\n\
- Next turn: Play Forest → have {3}{G}{U}\n\
- Cast **Trufflesnout** ({2}{G}), choose **gain 4 life** → to **17**\n\
- On turn 6: Cast **Ormos** if possible, discard three different cards, draw three\n\
\n\
But if the Hydra attacks again, I'm at 7 — then dead on turn 7.\n\
\n\
I need a board presence fast.\n\
\n\
