      "reasoning": "It's turn 5 — critical turn.\n\
\n\
I drew **Library Larcenist**, a 1/2 flier for {2}{U} with \"whenever this attacks, draw a card\" — great value engine.\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- 13 life\n\
- 4 untapped Forests and 1 Island → {4}{G}{U}\n\
- Land drop available\n\
\n\
Hand:\n\
- Irresistible Prey ({G})\n\
- Library Larcenist ({2}{U})\n\
- Ormos, Archive Keeper, Somberwald Stag ({3}{G})\n\
- Tome Anima ({3}{U})\n\
- Trufflesnout ({2}{G})\n\
\n\
Best play:\n\
- Play the **Forest** first (land drop)\n\
- Then cast **Trufflesnout** ({2}{G}) to gain 4 life → **17 life**\n\
\n\
**Why Trufflesnout?**\n\
- Life gain is essential — I'm at 13, next attack could be lethal\n\
- It’s the best rate for survival: a 2/2 that gives me 4 life\n\
- Gaining life helps against tempo and burn\n\
\n\
Alternative: cast **Tome Anima** first so it triggers when I cast a second creature. But I can only cast one creature now — unless I cast Trufflesnout first, then something else, but Tome Anima costs {3}{U}, Trufflesnout {2}{G} — both high.\n\
\n\
But if I cast Trufflesnout first, and later cast Library Larcenist or a second creature, Tome Anima triggers — gains flash, haste, and trample.\n\
\n\
So sequence:\n\
- Play land\n\
- Cast Trufflesnout\n\
- Hold off on other creatures to keep the trigger open\n\
\n\
Somberwald Stag is a 3/3 for {3}{G} — better body, but no life gain.\n\
\n\
At 13 life, **survival first**.\n\
\n\
So: **Play Forest, cast Trufflesnout, gain 4 life**.\n\
\n\
I play **Forest** first.\n\
\n\
\n\
