      "reasoning": "My opponent used **Benevolent Hydra**’s ability:  \n\
{tap}, Remove a +1/+1 counter: Put a +1/+1 counter on another target creature you control.  \n\
They targeted **Servant of the Scale** — which now goes from 4/4 to **5/5**.\n\
\n\
But wait — the battlefield now shows **Benevolent Hydra 5/5** — down from 6/6.\n\
\n\
And **Servant of the Scale** still has two +1/+1 counters — so becomes 5/5?\n\
\n\
Yes: base 2/2 +3 counters → 5/5.\n\
\n\
So they now have:\n\
- **Benevolent Hydra**: 5/5 flying, trample\n\
- **Servant of the Scale**: 5/5\n\
\n\
Both massive threats.\n\
\n\
Next attack will be lethal if unchecked — 5+5 = 10 trample damage minimum.\n\
\n\
I’m at 17 — I can take one full hit, maybe two with blocks.\n\
\n\
But I have no blockers yet.\n\
\n\
I must cast **Ormos** ASAP.\n\
\n\
I have: 5 lands (all tapped), hand: Dawntreader Elk, Library Larcenist, Ormos, Archive Keeper, Somberwald Stag, Tome Anima\n\
\n\
Next turn, I can:\n\
- Play a land (if I have one) — but I may be stuck at 5\n\
- Cast **Ormos** for {4}{G}{U} — need 6 lands\n\
\n\
So I must pray to draw a sixth land.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, **Dawntreader Elk** can sacrifice to fetch a Forest — but it costs {G} and entering tapped.\n\
\n\
But it’s a 2/2 body now.\n\
\n\
Still, I need 6 lands.\n\
\n\
Best play: survive.\n\
\n\
Pass priority to let the ability resolve.\n\
\n\
Here we go.\n\
\n\
