\n\
If I block:\n\
- Trufflesnout takes 6 damage -> dies\n\
- Servant takes 2 damage, survives\n\
\n\
I take no combat damage because Trufflesnout is blocking — but after first strike or regular damage?\n\
\n\
No first strike.\n\
\n\
Both deal damage simultaneously.\n\
\n\
Servant deals 6 to me (trample? No — it's not flying or trample — only the Hydra has trample).\n\
\n\
Wait — **Servant of the Scale** does **not** have trample.\n\
\n\
So I take **6 damage** regardless of blocking — the full power is assigned to me.\n\
\n\
Blocking does nothing — Trufflesnout dies, I still take 6 damage.\n\
\n\
Better to **not block** — preserve the body for future attacks and value.\n\
\n\
Yes — if I don't block:\n\
- No blockers\n\
- I take 6 damage (from 17 to 11)\n\
- Trufflesnout survives\n\
\n\
Then I can attack next turn.\n\
\n\
Even better, when I cast a second creature, **Tome Anima** triggers.\n\
\n\
So I **do not block**.\n\
\n\
I choose not to block.\n\
\n\
