      "reasoning": "Now the life total updates — I am at **13 life** (17 - 4? Wait, it says 13).\n\
\n\
I attacked for 3 earlier, opponent at 22 → 19.\n\
\n\
They attack with 6/6, deal 6 — I should be at 11.\n\
\n\
But game shows 13.\n\
\n\
This is inconsistent.\n\
\n\
Earlier I was at 17, took 6 — should be 11.\n\
\n\
But it shows 13.\n\
\n\
There’s a damage tracking bug.\n\
\n\
I was incorrectly marked at 17 after the Trufflesnout life gain — but I was actually at 13 (19 - 6).\n\
\n\
This is a mess.\n\
\n\
I think the true state is:\n\
- After blocking the 6/6, I should have been at 16\n\
- Game said 13\n\
- Trufflesnout gave +4 → 17\n\
- Took 6 damage → 11\n\
\n\
But system shows 13.\n\
\n\
I must trust the displayed total: **13 life**.\n\
\n\
I still have **Trufflesnout**, **Sylvan Brushstrider**, and hand full.\n\
\n\
I’ll pass to end the turn.\n\
\n\
I've survived — against the odds and bugs.\n\
\n\
Like in Malmö, where the judge overrode a corrupted game — we kept playing.\n\
\n\
I’m still in this.\n\
\n\
I pass.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
