      "reasoning": "I drew **Thriving Grove** — a dual land that enters tapped and can produce {G} or one mana of a non-green color.\n\
\n\
Perfect — exactly what I needed.\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- 4 untapped lands: Forest x3, Island\n\
- One land drop available\n\
\n\
I can and must play **Thriving Grove**.\n\
\n\
It will enter tapped — so I can’t use it for mana this turn, but it sets me up for permanents.\n\
\n\
After that, I can cast:\n\
- **Dawntreader Elk** ({1}{G}) — possible\n\
- **Library Larcenist** ({2}{U}) — possible\n\
- **Tome Anima** ({3}{U}) — possible\n\
- **Ormos** — {4}{G}{U}, needs 6 lands — not yet\n\
\n\
Best plays:\n\
- Play **Thriving Grove**\n\
- Then cast **Library Larcenist** ({2}{U}) — 1/2 flying, “whenever this attacks, draw a card” — great card advantage\n\
- Or cast **Tome Anima** to set up flash\n\
\n\
Priority: set up **Tome Anima** triggers.\n\
\n\
If I cast **Dawntreader Elk** first, it doesn’t trigger Tome Anima because it’s the first creature.\n\
\n\
But if I cast **Library Larcenist** first, then **Dawntreader Elk**, Tome Anima triggers — gains flash, haste, trample.\n\
\n\
So best:\n\
- Play **Thriving Grove** (tapped)\n\
- Cast **Library Larcenist** ({2}{U})\n\
- Then **Dawntreader Elk** ({1}{G})\n\
- Tome Anima triggers — can now attack\n\
\n\
Attack with all three creatures:\n\
- Brushstrider 3/2\n\
- Trufflesnout 2/2 (must be blocked by aura)\n\
- Larcenist 1/2 flying\n\
- Dawntreader Elk 2/2 — if I cast it\n\
\n\
But I may not have enough mana.\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- 3 Forest, 1 Island → {3}{G}{U}\n\
- After playing Thriving Grove (tapped), I have same\n\
\n\
Casting **Library Larcenist** ({2}{U}) — leaves {G} and one floating\n\
\n\
Then I can’t cast **Dawntreader Elk** ({1}{G}) — only {2} total, need {1}{G} — I have it?\n\
\n\
{3}{G}{U} - {2}{U} = {1}{G} — yes, exactly enough.\n\
\n\
So:\n\
- Play Thriving Grove (land)\n\
- Cast Library Larcenist ({2}{U})\n\
- Cast Dawntreader Elk ({1}{G})\n\
- Tome Anima triggers — gains flash, haste, trample\n\
- Attack with three creatures — possibly 3+2+2 = 7 unblocked, Larcenist can fly over\n\
\n\
But Trufflesnout has **Irresistible Prey** — only dies if blocked.\n\
\n\
So I can attack with it — they must block or it hits.\n\
\n\
Likely trade.\n\
\n\
But the life gain from Trufflesnout is gone.\n\
\n\
Still, 5+ damage possible.\n\
\n\
I could hold Larcenist for later draw.\n\
\n\
But I need tempo.\n\
\n\
Best: cast **Tome Anima** now, then **Library Larcenist**.\n\
\n\
Tome Anima ({3}{U}) — I have {3}{G}{U} — enough.\n\
\n\
Then I can cast Larcenist.\n\
\n\
But after Tome Anima, I have {G} — not enough for Larcenist ({2}{U}).\n\
\n\
So I can’t cast both.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Play land, cast Larcenist, pass — hold Elk for next turn\n\
- Play land, cast Tome Anima, pass — hold Larcenist\n\
\n\
Better to cast **Library Larcenist** — flying, card draw, tempo.\n\
\n\
Tome Anima can wait.\n\
\n\
I do:\n\
- Play **Thriving Grove**\n\
- Cast **Library Larcenist**\n\
\n\
Then attack.\n\
\n\
I play **Thriving Grove** first.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
