      "reasoning": "My opponent played **Rousing Read**? Not on the stack.\n\
\n\
Battlefield shows **Rousing Read** still on the battlefield — so they didn’t cast it.\n\
\n\
But they tapped both attackers.\n\
\n\
So they are attacking with:\n\
- **Benevolent Hydra** 5/5 flying, trample\n\
- **Servant of the Scale** 6/6\n\
\n\
Total potential damage: 11, trample.\n\
\n\
I have no flyers.\n\
\n\
Blocking options:\n\
- Let **Library Larcenist** (1/2 sick) block Hydra — dies, takes 5 from trample (5 damage)\n\
- Let **Trufflesnout** (2/2) block Servant — dies, takes 4 (6 - 2)\n\
\n\
But Servant is 6/6, Trufflesnout 2/2 — Trufflesnout takes 6, dies, I take 4.\n\
\n\
Then Hydra hits — trample, 5 damage.\n\
\n\
Total: 5 (from Servant) + 5 (from Hydra) = 10 — I die from 13 to 3.\n\
\n\
Can’t block both.\n\
\n\
Best block:\n\
- Block **Hydra** with **Library Larcenist** — Larcenist dies, I take 4 trample (5 damage - 1 blocked)\n\
- Let **Servant** through — 6 damage\n\
- Total: 4 + 6 = 10 — still die\n\
\n\
No good blocks.\n\
\n\
I take full 11 trample damage.\n\
\n\
I go from 13 to **2 life**.\n\
\n\
Still alive.\n\
\n\
I must survive.\n\
\n\
No beneficial blocks.\n\
\n\
I **do not block** — let all damage through.\n\
\n\
I survive at 2 life.\n\
\n\
I pass priority.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
