- **Library Larcenist** 1/2 flying\n\
- **Oneirophage** 1/2 flying (just entered, sick)\n\
\n\
**Oneirophage** is sick — cannot attack.\n\
\n\
So I can attack with:\n\
- **Library Larcenist** — flying, will draw a card when it attacks\n\
- **Sylvan Brushstrider** — 3/2\n\
- **Trufflesnout** — 2/2, if blocked, I draw\n\
\n\
Best to attack with all three.\n\
\n\
My opponent has:\n\
- **Benevolent Hydra** 5/5 flying, tapped\n\
- **Servant of the Scale** 6/6, tapped\n\
\n\
So:\n\
- Hydra can block flyers\n\
- Servant blocks ground\n\
\n\
Likely blocks:\n\
- Hydra blocks **Library Larcenist** — trading 1 for 5, I draw a card\n\
- Servant blocks **Sylvan Brushstrider** — 3 for 6, I take 3 from trample? No trample on Servant\n\
- **Trufflesnout** blocked — I draw\n\
\n\
But Servant has no trample — so if it blocks Brushstrider, only 3 damage assigned.\n\
\n\
Then Trufflesnout must be blocked — so likely overblocked.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, they let Trufflesnout through — 2 damage.\n\
\n\
Best I can get:\n\
- 2 (Trufflesnout) + 3 (Brushstrider) + 1 (Larcenist) = 6 damage, I draw two cards\n\
\n\
I go from 4 to 8 on the life counter — good.\n\
\n\
Cast **Tome Anima** or **Dawntreader Elk** next turn with draws.\n\
\n\
I attack with **all** available — Brushstrider, Trufflesnout, Library Larcenist.\n\
\n\
**Oneirophage** holds back.\n\
\n\
Let's go.\n\
\n\
**Every game has a turning point. This is mine.**\n\
