      "reasoning": "I drew **Narcolepsy** — a {1}{U} aura that taps a creature at the beginning of each upkeep if it's untapped.\n\
\n\
I also see **Oneirophage** has +1/+1 — because when **Library Larcenist** attacked, I drew a card, triggering Oneirophage's ability.\n\
\n\
So now Oneirophage is 2/3 with flying.\n\
\n\
My attackers dealt damage:\n\
- Sylvan Brushstrider 3/2 — likely blocked by Servant, died\n\
- Trufflesnout 2/2 — must be blocked, died\n\
- Library Larcenist 1/2 — likely blocked by Hydra, died\n\
\n\
But I drew a card — Narcolepsy.\n\
\n\
Opponent is at 14 - 6 = **8 life** — perfect.\n\
\n\
Now it's my opponent's turn.\n\
\n\
They attack with:\n\
- **Benevolent Hydra** 5/5 flying, trample\n\
- **Servant of the Scale** 6/6\n\
\n\
Total 11 damage, trample.\n\
\n\
I am at 4.\n\
\n\
Blocking:\n\
- I have **Oneirophage** 2/3 flying — can block Hydra\n\
- If I block, I take 3 trample (5 - 2)\n\
- Servant hits for 6 → total 9 damage — I die (4 → -5)\n\
\n\
If I don't block:\n\
- Take 5 (Hydra) + 6 (Servant) = 11 → die\n\
\n\
No way to survive.\n\
\n\
But I must block Hydra with Oneirophage — trade the flyer, reduce damage to 3 + 6 = 9 — still die, but at least I remove a threat.\n\
\n\
Still lethal.\n\
\n\
Unless...\n\
\n\
Wait — I have **Narcolepsy** in hand.\n\
\n\
Can I cast it?\n\
\n\
Mana: Thriving Grove untapped — {G} or {U}\n\
\n\
Narcolepsy is {1}{U} — I can cast it — produce {U} from Thriving Grove.\n\
\n\
So yes.\n\
\n\
Best play:\n\
- Don't block\n\
- Cast **Narcolepsy** on **Benevolent Hydra**\n\
- It deals 5 damage, I take 5 — go to -1? 4 - 5 = -1\n\
\n\
Wait.\n\
\n\
4 - 5 = -1 — dead.\n\
\n\
Unless trample assigns minimally.\n\
\n\
Hydra has trample.\n\
\n\
I can assign 2 to Oneirophage and 3 to me.\n\
\n\
Same.\n\
\n\
No blocker?\n\
\n\
I have no creature that can survive.\n\
\n\
I am dead.\n\
\n\
Unless Narcolepsy saves me.\n\
\n\
If I cast Narcolepsy on Hydra, it doesn't remove trample damage already being dealt.\n\
\n\
The damage is on the stack.\n\
\n\
Casting Narcolepsy now won't stop the combat damage.\n\
\n\
So I die.\n\
\n\
But let's see.\n\
\n\
Combat damage is about to resolve.\n\
\n\
I have one last move.\n\
\n\
I can cast **Narcolepsy** on **Benevolent Hydra** to tap it, but it's already tapped from attacking.\n\
\n\
And it won't prevent damage.\n\
\n\
So no.\n\
\n\
I must take the damage.\n\
\n\
Best: block with **Oneirophage** on **Hydra** — I take 3 trample.\n\
\n\
Then **Servant** deals 6.\n\
\n\
Total 9 — I die.\n\
\n\
Draw? No.\n\
\n\
But I have **Tome Anima**.\n\
\n\
If I cast a creature after this, it gains flash, haste, trample.\n\
\n\
But I'm dead.\n\
\n\
No.\n\
\n\
I think I cannot survive.\n\
\n\
But I must try.\n\
\n\
I have an idea.\n\
\n\
Cast **Narcolepsy** on **Hydra** — it's {1}{U} — I can do it.\n\
\n\
Then, when combat damage resolves, Hydra deals 5, trample — 2 to Oneirophage, 3 to me.\n\
\n\
I go to 1.\n\
\n\
Servant deals 6 — I go to -5.\n\
\n\
Still dead.\n\
\n\
No.\n\
\n\
The only way is if Narcolepsy somehow prevents the attack — but it doesn't.\n\
\n\
I am at 4 life.\n\
\n\
2+6=8 direct damage.\n\
\n\
I die.\n\
\n\
But the game shows the opponent at 8 life — I dealt 6 damage.\n\
\n\
They can finish me.\n\
\n\
I have to accept it.\n\
\n\
But I have a hand full of gas.\n\
\n\
I pass.\n\
\n\
**You win this turn. But in my deck, the next game is never far. Reminds me of Kyoto — one loss, ten lessons.**",
